Z||000000||ROB MAC||06-30-2001||01:09 PM||||Set a code 42- cleaned distributor- tested module- regreased and re-assembled- new rotor<BR>Car ran fine for a few days . Sometimes when the car hit a bump the check engine light would flicker. Went on the highway and the light would flicker on and off and the engine would miss or stumble slightly. No code set. Could it be a bad spark module?||||reg||1
Z||000001||DecadenceR||06-30-2001||01:22 PM||||I had the same problem a few weeks back.<BR>What i did was clean all the power cable contacts, and make sur they were really tight. Seemed to work for me. Hopefully your solution will be as simple.<BR>Also, what kind of motor do you have?||||reg||1
Z||000002||ROB MAC||06-30-2001||01:39 PM||||'84 2.5 . Had a clutch put in and electrical problems seemed to start right after that. I'll check power and grounds today.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ROB MAC||06-30-2001||10:55 PM||||Many thanks DecadenceR for pointing the way!<BR>I was all set to start replacing distributor parts when you said " Power cables". I found the power wire from positive battery to alternator had come loose from that plastic cover and was rubbing on the waterpump pulley. It wore through the fuse link wire and was causing the engine light to flicker and causing a miss. I spliced it and re-routed it up and over the alternator frame. ||||reg||1
